<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paolo Erizzo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1470">1470</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paolo Erizzo was the Venetian bailo, or governor, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euboea">Negroponte</a> (Chalkis) on Euboea when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> besieged it by land and sea in 1470. He defended the city until it was stormed in July and was killed after its fall; Venetian tradition says he was sawn in half. The loss of Negroponte was a heavy blow to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in its war with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p></div>
